 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nVersion parsing incorrectly handles ALL AS OF syntax\n\nWhen parsing version clauses with `ALL AS OF` syntax, the parser incorrectly processes the tokens, causing `ALL` to be treated as `AS OF` and vice versa.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should parse correctly but doesn't\nsql = \"SELECT * FROM table FOR SYSTEM_TIME ALL AS OF timestamp\"\nparsed = sqlglot.parse_one(sql)\nprint(parsed)\n\n# Expected: Version with kind=\"ALL\" \n# Actual: Version with kind=\"AS OF\" and expression=None\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when the parser encounters `ALL` followed by `AS OF` - it incorrectly matches the `ALL` token and then tries to parse `AS OF` as a type expression, leading to malformed version clauses.\n</issue>\n",
